## THE END-TO-END RUN — NOT USABLE, and the harness said so itself

Same cell, same contract as the certified baseline (convection side-64, 81 rounds,
taskset -c 1, live SuperLU in the same invocation):

    competitive_ratio  0.676619  ci95 [0.663005, 0.690933]     THIS RUN
    competitive_ratio  0.663058  ci95 [0.657063, 0.678674]     BASELINE (8e6816aa5)

Two reasons this establishes NOTHING about wall-clock, and both matter:

1. THE NULLS ARE BIASED, not merely imprecise. `all_null_ci95_span_unity=false` —
   the diagnostic added earlier today in 8e6816aa5, firing negative for the first time:

       candidate_A/A        0.986928  [0.957182, 1.009348]   spans unity
       control_A/A          0.993888  [0.979521, 1.017473]   spans unity
       candidate_live_pair  1.022261  [1.007147, 1.043525]   EXCLUDES unity
       live_A/A             1.015756  [1.002566, 1.026561]   EXCLUDES unity

   Two nulls have CIs entirely above 1.0. That is arm-order contamination, not
   sampling width, and it means the ratio above them is not trustworthy at this
   precision. Host load was 39.74 at the start of the window against ~20 for the
   baseline. This is exactly the distinction that diagnostic exists to draw, and it
   is drawing it against my own result.

2. EVEN AT FACE VALUE THE CIs OVERLAP: [0.663005, 0.690933] against
   [0.657063, 0.678674], overlapping on [0.663005, 0.678674]. Nothing is separated.

So: NO WALL-CLOCK CLAIM. The counted mechanism moved and is landed on that basis;
whether ~20% off the merge kernel's marginal cost is visible end-to-end on this cell
is UNMEASURED, and owes a run in a quiet window against the same baseline.

WHY IT MIGHT NOT SHOW even when measured cleanly, stated in advance so the next run
is read honestly: the merge kernel is one component of a factor-plus-16-solves job.
The `--convection-split` probe puts the SOLVE at 33-35% of that job, so the factor is
roughly two thirds, and the merge inner loop is only part of the factor. A 19.9% cut
in that inner loop's marginal cost is bounded well below 19.9% of the job — plausibly
a few percent, which is the same order as this cell's null width. The counted row is
the strong evidence here; the end-to-end row may never separate.

